3. Sensitive Personal Information
We will only process Sensitive Personal Information where it is necessary for the purposes of complying with our legal obligations or exercising specific rights as permitted by law. 
Sensitive Personal Information is any information that reveals your race, ethnic origin, religious beliefs, mental or physical health condition or diagnosis, sex life or sexual orientation, citizenship or citizenship status, genetic or biometric data, personal information of a known child, or precise geographic data. For example, if you consented to and enabled precise geographic location when using our App or Site, we may use this information to provide you with Great Clips® salon locations and distances to such locations.  If you did not consent, we will use approximate geographic data or geographic data based on your input, such as a zip code.
When installing our App or in subsequent uses, you may have given the app permission to access the precise geolocation data from your phone’s operating system.  If you wish to modify this setting, you may do so through your phone’s settings menu.  Please review your operating system instructions as they may be different for each operating systems and version.
Our Site and App are designed for a general audience and are not directed to children.  We do not knowingly collect or solicit personal information from children under the age of 18.

4. Your Rights Under Privacy Laws
The Right to Know. You have the right to know about and request the Personal Information we have collected, disclosed, or sold about you in the preceding 12 months. You may make such a request up to twice in a 12-month span. Please note that there are circumstances in which we may not be able to comply with your request pursuant to Privacy Laws, including when we cannot verify your request and/or when there is a conflict with our own obligations to comply with other legal or regulatory requirements. We will notify you following submission of your request if this is the case.
The Right to Deletion of Your Personal Information. You have the right to request that we delete certain Personal Information that we have collected. Please note that there are circumstances in which we may not be able to comply with your request pursuant to Privacy Laws, including when we cannot verify your request and/or when there is a conflict with our own obligations to comply with other legal or regulatory requirements. We will notify you following submission of your request if this is the case.
The Right to Opt-Out. You have a right under Privacy Laws to opt-out of the sale or sharing of your personal information or targeted advertising. The process for exercising this right is described below under Sale or Sharing of Information and Your Right to Opt-Out. 
The Right to Non-Discrimination. You have a right under Privacy Laws not to be discriminated against for the exercise of your other rights. This includes the right not to be denied goods or services, not to be charged different rates for goods or services, and not to receive a different level or quality of goods or services from us for your exercise of your privacy rights under Privacy Laws.
The Right to Correct Inaccurate Personal Information.  You have a right under Privacy Laws to correct inaccurate personal data we may have about you. If you would like to request this right, please submit a request via our Privacy Webform and provide all required information, including detailing the incorrect information you would like corrected.  Please note that there are circumstances in which we may not be able to comply with your request pursuant to Privacy Laws, including when we cannot verify your request and/or when there is a conflict with our own obligations to comply with other legal or regulatory requirements. We will notify you following submission of your request if this is the case.
The Right to Appeal. You may have a right under Privacy Laws to appeal our decision on a prior privacy request.  This right is available only with respect to an already completed request.  Please note that there are circumstances in which we may not be able to comply with your request pursuant to Privacy Laws, including when we cannot verify your request and/or when there is a conflict with our own obligations to comply with other legal or regulatory requirements. We will notify you following submission of your request if this is the case.
5. Exercising Your Rights Under Privacy Laws

    Right to Know and Right to Deletion. You can make a request by accessing the Privacy Webform or by calling our toll-free number at 1-888-914-9661, and entering pin 143565. The link will take you to an interactive webform that you can complete and submit to make the request that we will then verify; if you use the telephone number, you will be guided through a process that will allow you to submit a request, and the level of verification will depend on the request being submitted. We may follow-up with you to obtain additional verification information, as needed. You may also obtain a written form (with a pre-paid envelope) at a salon location in California and Virginia. 
    Opt-Out of Sale or Sharing of Information and Targeted Advertising. Use the Privacy Webform to submit a request to Opt-Out of Sale/Share and Targeted Advertising.

        In addition to the webform request, you will also need to customize your cookie settings on the Site and App.

            Great Clips uses technologies on our website which gather personal information. And, like most companies with an online presence, we share some of that information with our cookie vendors to make sure we deliver the best information to you. This sharing of cookies may be considered a “sale” or “sharing” under Privacy Laws.   If you want to Opt-out of Targeted Advertising cookies, or other cookies that are not necessary for the performance of the website, you may do so by accessing our Cookie Preferences Center (also available via the Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information link in the Site footer or App settings) and adjusting your preferences for that web domain or App instance. If you opt-out, we will wait at least 12 months before asking you if we may sell or share your Personal Information.

            Please note: Clearing your browser cookies at any time will undo preferences saved through this process. To re-save preferences, please return to this screen after clearing your cookies. Also, please note that the option selected here will only apply to the device you are currently using. You may also opt out of advertising cookies from any other devices you use to access our website or mobile applications.
            We recognize Global Privacy Control (GPC) signals enabled by customers on their web browser or web browser extension to customize and honor cookie preferences. For more information about GPC, please visit Global Privacy Control.



        Lastly, visit NAI Opt Out or DAA Opt Out to learn about other methods to opt out of interest-based advertising. Both organizations operate a centralized registry that displays and manages opt-out preferences for participating advertising-technology providers.

        We will not deny, charge different prices for, or provide a different level or quality of goods or services, if you choose to exercise any of your privacy rights. 


    Right to Correct Personal Information. Use the Privacy Webform to submit a request to correct inaccurate Personal Information. 
    Right to Appeal. Use the Privacy Webform to submit a request to appeal a prior decision on a privacy request.  Please note that this right is available once such a decision is complete, and you are notified of our decision.  In order to submit a request to appeal through the webform, you will be required to provide the previous request ID referenced in email communications related to the request being appealed.


6. Verification Process
The verification process varies slightly depending on what right you are exercising. However, you can exercise your rights as follows:

    You are not required to create an account to exercise your rights; 
    You can make a request by accessing the Privacy Webform (or calling our toll-free line at 1-888-914-9661, pin 143565 or mailing in a paper form, in which case such request will be inputted on your  behalf); 
    You will be asked to indicate your residency; 
    You must then indicate which request you wish to exercise based upon the list of options presented:

        To request to opt-out of the sale or sharing of your Personal Information/opt out of targeted advertising, provide your first name, last name, phone number, and email, then you must click the verification link in your email for your request to proceed. 
        To request deletion of your Personal Information, provide your first name, last name, email, phone number, country, and state of residency, then click the verification link in your email for your request to proceed. 
        To request access to your specific Personal Information and categorized information, provide your first name, last name, email, phone number, country, and state of residency, then click the verification link in your email for your request to proceed. 
        These steps may be updated or amended. If they are, we will describe the updated verification process in this policy.




